<h1>About this project</h1>
<p>
  The Alumni Tracking System is the term project of <strong>Web Programming</strong>
  (Istanbul University, Management Information Systems, Fall 2026). It keeps a register of
  students and graduates, lets alumni publish job postings, and lets users apply to them.
</p>

<h2>How it is built</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Back end:</strong> Node.js with Express — one process, non-blocking I/O, one language on both sides.</li>
  <li><strong>Database:</strong> PostgreSQL — real foreign keys, real unique constraints, strict types.</li>
  <li><strong>ORM:</strong> Sequelize — it writes the SQL, and the SQL stays readable.</li>
  <li><strong>Views:</strong> EJS — HTML for people, JSON for programs, one model behind both.</li>
  <li><strong>Everything runs with:</strong> <code>docker compose up</code>.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Weakness of each choice</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Node.js: a single thread — one heavy CPU task blocks every other request.</li>
  <li>PostgreSQL: heavier to set up and to change than a document store; every change needs a migration.</li>
</ul>

